 lens the quality is as good  as the main shooter but the perspective  it provides is very unique the  distortion is surprisingly minimal due  to software correction and for most  people even those who have actual  cameras this will be wider than other  lenses at they own I own seven cameras  and dozens of lenses but I used my phone  more often for photos because it's  always there so the camera quality  really matters to me this means that I  always try to own the best smartphone  camera available and through the years  that's been the iPhone switching to the  Samsung I wasn't giving up quality like  I was in the past in our own blind  comparison the sn+ beat out the iPhone  overall and watching zone of text X  comparison I chose the iPhone as my  preference but the sn+ was very close  there were three things that bug me  though first pin ramus are now shot  using the wide-angle lens this gives you  a different perspective but can really  mess up your images second for portraits  you now have to use the standard lens  and set at the telephoto now this is  great to show more of your scene and  helps in low-light but Samsung is the  king of giving us options why not let us  choose which lens is better for a  particular situation both for portraits  and panoramas the third is the shutter  lag Apple was able to fix this since  it's a 12 processor with our smart HDR  is constantly taking a bunch of images  which does introduce some more noise but  you never miss a shot the sand plus at  times can have close to a second of  delays so I didn't miss some shots of my  kids that I wouldn't have with iPhone as  far as video and my quality they have  also made some great strides but from my  pro videography perspective the overall  quality is still behind Apple this is a  microphone quality from the galaxy s 10  Plus this is a microphone quality of the  iPhone 10 s max stabilization is great  and the super smooth video is really  cool but it's limited to 1080p almost no  reviewers actually went into the HDR 10  plus recording feature and that's  because it's not really usable for most  if you want to actually edit and upload  your videos it's mostly only good if you  want to watch the videos on the phone  itself one video feature I missed is 24  frames per second recording on the  iPhone which helps in low-light and is  great if you want to match with other  camera footage speakers have always been  the weak point for Samsung but not  anymore the stem plus doesn't sound as  good as the iPhone and yes I did enable  Dobey ammos but it's closed and much  louder  [Music]  honestly I would choose the s10 speakers  any day since the extra volume comes in  really handy when listening to a podcast  or video that's too quiet speaking of  watching videos oh man the experience is  fantastic not only is the HDR both  brighter and more contrast II but the  high-res display with the ability of  stream 1440p instead of 1080 really  makes the image pop not only that but  the small cutout is way less noticeable  and since its offset I can flip the  phone and so it's at the bottom right  next to my palm and I notice it even  less that better video viewing  experience also drains more of the  battery but since the sm+ has a larger  battery i still get about 30 minutes to  an hour more screen on time than the  iPhone now let's touch on the ultrasonic  fingerprint reader the tech is super  cool and we couldn't fully in our  fingerprint hacking video but actually  using it was a hit or miss I tried  different pressures angles lengths to  leave my finger on it and it just wasn't  consistent I then thought to try to  register the same fingerprint again and  it worked much better the next day Lou  put out a video on this and I was glad  that it wasn't just me I added a third  print and it got even better it's still  not perfect but better than before  I think Samsung can tweak this over time  and I know the text will improve in the  future but for now it's definitely not  as easy of space ID there's one thing  that I don't love about the SN plus an  actual day to day use and that's the  curved edges yes it looks great for  product shots and makes the phone  slimmer so it's more comfortable to use  in the hand but I would often  accidentally change YouTube videos and  randomly like Instagram photos  personally I prefer the standard flat  design of the s10 II and I would take  that if they offered it with this larger  size so we talked a lot about hardware  now let's touch on the software the new  one UI is an improvement from the past  but Samsung still has a way to go with  speed and reliability compared to one  plus I ended up changing my icons on the  keyboard when everything from my 1 plus  60 is great out of the box and that  ability to customize everything is the  beauty of Android wear iOS is more  lockdown but on another hand iOS does  have a lot fewer app crashes glitches  and bloatware notifications on the S 10  were annoying with games trying to get  me to play apps wanting to be downloaded  and Amazon wanting me to shop all of  this can be customized and fixed but  with the iPhone you don't have to now on  the plus side I'm always surprised by  the extra features I notice in apps that  I use most often  I love Facebook's messenger  little pop-up overlay and YouTube's  picture-in-picture mode so it's all of  the great hardware features and  improvements of the s10 over the iPhone  why did I end up switching back it's  basically the whole Apple ecosystem  holding me in if it wasn't I would  switch but I left my Apple watch and  also having continuity with my max I use  airdrop almost daily and forced touch  really speeds things up for me along  with that I didn't realize how much  losing iMessage would actually affect me  Apple is great I'm making the products  work seamlessly which is nice but it  also sucks because it locks you in if I  didn't need Mac OS every day for work  and I didn't own and love the Apple  watch I would have not switched back to  the iPhone Destin plus is in my opinion  the best phone on the market it's not  perfect but it's the closest thing you  can get to it if you're an iPhone user  that's not too locked in and thinking of  switching do it and if you're using  Android already and one upgrade it's a  no-brainer  thanks for watching if you want to see  more videos like this one including our  galaxy SN II review click that little  circle above to subscribe and check out  our other SN videos including these ones  this man max max tech and I'll see you  in the next video  [Music]
 

